# Project: Flyrank Ai

## Stack
- Frontend: Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS
- Backend: Python 3.11+ with FastAPI
- Database: PostgreSQL (planned)
- AI: LLM API calls made from the backend only (never expose API keys to the browser)

## Folder structure
- `frontend/` – Next.js app
- `backend/` – FastAPI app
- `docs/` – project notes and decisions

## Conventions
- Commits follow Conventional Commits: feat, fix, docs, chore, refactor, test, style
- TypeScript: strict mode, no `any`, functional React components with hooks
- Python: type hints on all functions, follow PEP 8, use Pydantic models for request/response
- Name files and folders in kebab-case (frontend) and snake_case (backend)
- Secrets live in `.env` files and are never committed
- Keep functions small; add a short comment explaining *why*, not *what*

## FLyrank Ai
- Explain changes in simple terms before applying them
- Prefer small, focused edits over large rewrites
- Ask before adding new dependencies
## Rules learned from the prompt drill
- Feature specs live in `docs/<feature>-spec.md`. Read the spec and show a
  plan (files → steps → test cases) before writing any code.
- Validation lives in pure functions in `frontend/src/lib/validate-*.ts`
  with Vitest tests. Always trim text input before validating or saving;
  never rely on the HTML `required` attribute alone.
- Never use `as` casts on data from localStorage, JSON or APIs. Check the
  shape at runtime first.
- Form inputs need `<label htmlFor>`, `aria-invalid` and
  `aria-describedby`; success/status messages need `role="status"`.
- Only touch files the task names. Never edit `frontend/src/app/page.tsx`
  unless asked.
- After any change in `/frontend`, run `npm test`, `npm run lint`,
  `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build`, and paste the raw output, not a
  summary.